  "behavior": [
    "ComboBox.setItemData uses one direct native call and supports text, value, enabled state, separator and icon. Length mismatch with no explicit bound and embedded NUL are checked before calling C.",
    "ComboBox.getItem copies display text and four scalars. Invalid indices and failed text copies preserve the old tuple. Captured text remains usable after updating or closing the widget.",
    "XUI keeps the native pUser contract at the C interface. The language record projection leaves pUser NULL.",
    "In 1000 warmed reads, the language makes one owned-text allocation per item. The C comparison reads borrowed text. In 1000 identical, unchanged three-row writes, the language makes one temporary record allocation per call. C supplies its record array directly and the native equality fast path allocates nothing.",
    "Accepted writes also keep five sequence read pins during projection, scan text for NUL and traverse the columns. Native changed-item text storage is allocated when needed. Checked state, ownership and scope overhead were not measured in CPU time.",
    "The native fixture initially passed functional assertions but leaked its mock rendering target. It now frees that target in cleanup, and the qualified native fixtures verify overall XRT heap balance."
  ],
